WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.588
Welcome to Psychology of UX. Work in a group to compare two interface features

00:00:05.588 --> 00:00:11.175
using psychological principles and research. Each student also keeps an individual reflective journal.

00:00:11.175 --> 00:00:15.420
Your group literature review is two thousand words, plus or minus ten percent. Use

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:19.665
APA 7 referencing and at least six peer reviewed articles. The reference list and

00:00:19.665 --> 00:00:23.910
appendices do not count towards the word limit.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:27.812
Use the resources to read, listen and watch. Library links take you to IADT

00:00:27.812 --> 00:00:31.713
services, where you may need to sign in. Evaluate the research evidence rather than

00:00:31.713 --> 00:00:35.615
treating every resource as equal.

00:00:35.615 --> 00:00:40.320
Keep your own record of contributions, decisions and feedback. Reflect on your performance and

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:45.025
your next step. Your individual critical reflection is five hundred words. The group shares

00:00:45.025 --> 00:00:49.730
its output, but each person explains their own learning.

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:54.345
The rubric separates the group research and analysis from individual reflection and contribution. You

00:00:54.345 --> 00:00:58.960
can review a personal log alongside the individual criterion. Formative feedback helps you identify

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:03.575
what to improve before submission.
